      ":question/problem": "![](images/6a/6ae03cd157dcd315fd828475645b465fcce5c2b3f414aa24933405bea4fc7e1a.png)\n\nConsider the following functions:\n\n$f(x, y) = (x + p, y + q), g(x, y) = (\\frac{1}{4}x, \\frac{1}{4}y)$\n\nThe function $f(x, y)$ is applied to $C$, and then $g(x, y)$ is applied to the result. The image of $C$ under this sequence of transformations is $C^{\u2032}$. What is $p + q$?"
